# Source images. The site loads only img/ — those are the optimised copies
# (5.8 MB -> 600 KB). These originals stay on your machine so you can re-crop
# or re-export later; they just don't belong in the repo or on the server.
# Regenerate an img/ file from its original with sips, e.g.:
#   sips -Z 1400 header.png -s format jpeg -s formatOptions 72 --out img/header.jpg
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp

# Cloudflare Pages build output — rebuilt on every deploy
dist/

# Machine noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT ignore raw/ — it looks big but it is load-bearing.
# Those bhavcopy zips are the archive the whole pipeline rests on. scan.py skips
# any date already on disk, so keeping them committed means the daily job fetches
# ONE 195 KB file instead of re-downloading a year from NSE on every run.
# They are excluded from the live site by the Cloudflare build command, not here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
